{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Et.</b> Both masculine and feminine, like lekha, gam bekha, ve-ʿimmakha, ve-ʾittakha; but ve-ʾattah is masculine alone." "<b>Hargeni.</b> Like heimiteni. Do this to me in Your righteousness and for my appeasement. This is the meaning of \"and if I have found favor in Your eyes.\"" "<b>Ve-al ʾerʾeh.</b> [That I not see] further the trouble I am in. And there is no need for a scribal emendation."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:17:14.031369736Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}